@page "/"

<PageTitle>Reporting Dashboard</PageTitle>

<h1>
    Problem statement and motivation
</h1>

<p>
    There is currently a high demand to generate new reports that can be distributed to 
    specific people for various departments and users in the company. There is legacy 
    infrastructure that has become difficult to maintain and is also not capable of adding 
    modern features like role-based access. Managers and executives just have to hope that 
    users don’t accidentally enter a URL that contains a sensitive report. The legacy 
    reporting structure also does not have centralized business logic. Different reports 
    running in different locations have logic and queries that do not necessarily align 
    with each other. Third party software like Power BI is built for this but comes with 
    recurring licensing costs. For a couple of users, managers find this acceptable, but 
    management also wants these reports accessible by a larger audience, which means that these 
    licensing costs add up. They need a system that will have role-based access, that has a 
    modern user interface, and that does not come with recurring licensing costs.
</p>